---
/**
 * Override of Starlight's `SiteTitle`, so the docs header shows the same
 * lockup as the standalone pages.
 *
 * Starlight's `logo` config option takes an image PATH, so it cannot
 * render an inline SVG — and an inline SVG is the whole point (see the
 * header of `WarrenLogo.astro`: the old `logo.png` carried an opaque
 * near-black background into a light-themed header). Overriding the
 * component is the supported way to put real markup there, so
 * `astro.config.mjs` sets `components.SiteTitle` to this file and no
 * longer sets `logo` at all.
 *
 * The target is `/` — the landing page — which is also where
 * `SiteHeader.astro` points the same lockup, so the brand behaves
 * identically inside and outside the docs. Starlight's default reads
 * `Astro.locals.starlightRoute.siteTitleHref` instead, which accounts for
 * `base` and for the active locale. Neither is configured here (the build
 * pins `BASE_URL=/` and the site is single-locale), and reading that
 * value would mean adding `@astrojs/starlight/locals` to the `types`
 * array in `tsconfig.json` — which resolves to Starlight's SOURCE and
 * fails `tsc` on its `virtual:starlight/*` imports. If a base path or a
 * second locale ever lands, switch to `siteTitleHref` and solve the
 * typing then.
 *
 * The visible wordmark inside `WarrenLogo` is this link's accessible
 * name, so there is no `sr-only` title span. Starlight's own default
 * renders one only because its logo is an image with an empty `alt`.
 */
import WarrenLogo from "./WarrenLogo.astro";
---

<a href="/" class="site-title sl-flex">
	<WarrenLogo size={26} />
</a>

<style>
	.site-title {
		align-items: center;
		color: var(--color-fg);
		text-decoration: none;
		white-space: nowrap;
		min-width: 0;
	}
</style>
